195
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:55,070
Maybe inside a given row of the table, you are attending everything to everything.

196
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:57,670
So, you have let's say a row based attention.

197
00:17:57,670 --> 00:18:07,950
Then you have also a column based attention where a given column is attending to other columns, to other rows, other values of the same column to get a sense of what is the distribution of values, right?

198
00:18:07,950 --> 00:18:14,470
So, that's also quadratic, but it's kind of quadratic in some band of the number of rows.

199
00:18:14,470 --> 00:18:19,310
The other one is kind of quadratic in the maybe the number of columns per table, not the total data.

200
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:30,950
And then you also have the attention across tables that again is highly structured, is not everything to everything, but it's just across the links that actually exist among the entities.

201
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:35,150
So, you basically have three different types of attention that is I would say highly structured.

202
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:46,110
So, you can process large amounts of tokens because it's not that any token in a database can attend to any other token as in text,

203
00:18:46,110 --> 00:18:50,390
but you are attending inside a row, inside a column, and across the tables.

